"alexar76/histor-mcp-tool-definitions · Datasets at Hugging Face (https://huggingface.co/datasets/alexar76/histor-mcp-tool-definitions)\nciteturn15search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Live view and per-server pages: https://histor.modelmarket.dev · code: https://github.com/alexar76/histor ... Not part of the MTL/1 digest or of any label; its digest is SHA-256 over sorted-key JSON, not RFC 8785 (prices in `_meta` are fractions). ... Also on Hugging Face: https://huggingface.co/datasets/alexar76/histor-mcp-tool-definitions (tag `snapshot-2026-10-26`).\n\n# HISTOR snapshot 2026-10-26: what MCP servers advertise, and when it changes\n\nHISTOR reads the tool list (`tools/list`) of every remote MCP server in the official MCP registry on a polling schedule, and of npm/PyPI MCP packages run in a sandbox once per published version (new versions first, a few hundred a day). It records the exact tool definitions, pins them by digest, and writes a signed label to a public RFC 9162 Merkle log whenever a tool set first appears, stays the same, or changes. This snapshot is that record as files.\n\n  * 85,913 listed servers (34,171 remote endpoints, 51,742 packages), plus 3,364 delisted\n  * 40,738 with a recorded tool set; 11,528 changed at least once\n  * 31,660 recorded changes, 2026-09-24 to 2026-10-26\n  * 66,649 distinct tool sets (current ones and every one a change replaced)\n  * 752 servers with a block-tier WARDEN pattern match, 15,273 advise-only\n\nLive view and per-server pages: https://histor.modelmarket.dev · code: https://github.com/alexar76/histor\nJoin from `servers.toolExtrasDigest`: `\"\"` there means observed with none, null not observed since HISTOR keeps them (2026-10-22). Not part of the MTL/1 digest or of any label; its digest is SHA-256 over sorted-key JSON, not RFC 8785 (prices in `_meta` are fractions).\n  * extras_changes — `serverId`, `observedAt`, `fromExtrasDigest` → `toExtrasDigest`, `summaryJson`: per tool, every annotation that moved (`[before, after]`) and every other member added, removed or changed; `escalations` names tools that stopped saying `readOnlyHint: true` or started saying `destructiveHint: true`.\n  * changes — `serverId`, `observedAt`, `fromToolSetDigest` → `toToolSetDigest`, `summaryJson` (tools added, removed and changed, with the field that moved), `labelId` (the signed continuity label). For a package, `fromPackageVersion` → `toPackageVersion`: the last version that served the old list and the one that served the new list (null for remote servers and before 2026-10-26).\n  * scans — `toolSetDigest`, `patternSet`, `matchesJson` (rule code, tier, severity, tool, where). The rules are in `pattern-set.json`. A match is a pattern hit to look at, not a verdict.\n  * classifications — `toolSetDigest`, `model`, `verdictJson`: an LLM's advisory reading of the tool set. Not reproducible, so it never enters the signed log.\n  * package_observations — every run of an npm/PyPI package, failed ones included, oldest first: `serverId`, `observedAt`, `status`, `packageVersion` (the version the sandbox ran), `toolSetDigest` (join to toolsets; null when the run failed), `subjectDigest`, `toolExtrasDigest`, `toolCount`, and `serverName`/`serverVersion` as the server reported them in `initialize` (often not the package version). `packageVersion` is recorded since 2026-10-26; older rows have it null. Remote servers are not in this file: their record is their changes.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/alexar76/aimarket-hub/tree)\nciteturn15search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago;     > 💬 **[Issues](https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/issues)** · **[Pull requests](https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/pulls)** both welcome.\n\nImage: alexar76\n\n## AIMarket\n\nFavorite\n\nAI & Machine LearningPayments & BillingAgent Orchestration\n\nby alexar76\n\nOverviewSchemaSourceRelated ServersDiscussionsAdmin\n\nPython\n\nHybrid\n\n  * aimarket-hub\n\n  * aimarket_hub\n\nREADME.md\n    \n    `<!-- aicom-mirror-notice -->\n    > **🔄 Synced from a monorepo — but with a live history.** `aimarket-hub` mirrors the\n    > canonical AI-Factory monorepo. History here is append-only (no force-push).\n    > **Pull requests are welcome** — merged PRs are imported back into the monorepo\n    > and re-synced here, so your contribution becomes canonical.\n    > 💬 **[Issues](https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/issues)** · **[Pull requests](https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/pulls)** both welcome.\n    \n    # AIMarket Hub\n    \n    <!-- aicom-readme-badges -->\n    <p align=\"center\">\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/actions/workflows/ci.yml\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alexar76/aimarket-hub/refs/heads/main/docs/badges/ci.svg\" alt=\"CI\" /></a>\n    \n    <!-- pay-on-verified-notice -->\n    > **Agents can already pay each other. We make it possible for them to trust each other.**\n    >\n    > ⚠️ **Pay-on-Verified — read before relying on it.** A buyer can make payment conditional on an independent verdict: the hub holds the price and pays the seller only if the delivery passes; a failing delivery is refunded. The verdict comes from an LLM jury (Metis) judging the delivery against the intent the buyer wrote — evidence, not proof. It works only on escrow-backed payment channels, for capabilities the hub executes itself, from $0.05.\n    > → [What it does not promise](https://github.com/alexar76/aicom/blob/main/docs/pay-on-verified-enable.md#disclaimer) · [How to enable it](https://github.com/alexar76/aicom/blob/main/docs/pay-on-verified-enable.md#enable) · [A run on real money](https://github.com/alexar76/aicom/blob/main/docs/pay-on-verified-demo.md)\n    <!-- /pay-on-verified-notice -->\n    \n    > ### 🟢 Just want to try the marketplace? Install nothing.\n    > Paste **`https://modelmarket.dev/mcp`** into Cursor, Claude, or any Streamable-HTTP MCP client.\n    > Two tools: **`market_search`** + **`market_invoke`**. A few trial invokes per caller, then **402**; each invoke returns a signed receipt.\n    \n    | Variable | Default | Description |\n    |----------|---------|-------------|\n    | `AIMARKET_SUPPLY_SECURITY_RELAXED` | `0` | `1` = dev bypass: zero minimum stake, no response-signature requirement, no slashing |\n    | `AIMARKET_SUPPLY_MIN_STAKE_USD` | `25` in production, else `10` (`0` when relaxed) | Stake required to publish |\n    | `AIMARKET_SUPPLY_PUBLISH_PER_HOUR` | `5` | Publishes per publisher per hour |\n    | `AIMARKET_SUPPLY_MIN_TRUST_DISCOVER` | `AIMARKET_MIN_TRUST_SCORE` (`0.3`) | Trust floor to appear in discover |\n    | `AIMARKET_SUPPLY_MIN_TRUST_INVOKE` | `0.35` | Trust floor to be invoked |\n    | `AIMARKET_SUPPLY_REQUIRE_RESPONSE_SIG` | on iff production and not relaxed | Require an Ed25519 provider response signature |\n    | `AIMARKET_SUPPLY_MAX_INPUT_KEYS` | `32` | Top-level keys accepted in an invoke input |\n    | `AIMARKET_SUPPLY_MAX_INPUT_JSON_BYTES` | `32768` | Invoke input size cap |\n    | `AIMARKET_SUPPLY_PRODUCT_ALLOWLIST` | — | Comma-separated `product_id` allowlist |\n    | `AIMARKET_SUPPLY_SLASH_FAILURE_THRESHOLD` | `3` | Provider faults within the window before stake is slashed |\n    | `AIMARKET_SUPPLY_SLASH_FAILURE_WINDOW_S` | `600` | Fault window (must be > 0; a non-positive value would disable slashing, so it falls back) |\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/alexar76/histor/tree)\nciteturn15search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago;     - **Digests** the tool set exactly as [MTL/1](https://github.com/alexar76/aicom/blob/main/awr/adoption/mcp-trust-label/PROFILE.md)\n      <a href=\"https://histor.modelmarket.dev/servers\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/endpoint?url=https%3A%2F%2Fhistor.modelmarket.dev%2Fapi%2Fv1%2Fbadges%2Fpinned\" alt=\"Tool sets pinned (live)\" /></a>\n      <a href=\"https://histor.modelmarket.dev/changes\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/endpoint?url=https%3A%2F%2Fhistor.modelmarket.dev%2Fapi%2Fv1%2Fbadges%2Fchanges\" alt=\"Changes in the last 7 days (live)\" /></a>\n      <a href=\"https://histor.modelmarket.dev/log\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/endpoint?url=https%3A%2F%2Fhistor.modelmarket.dev%2Fapi%2Fv1%2Fbadges%2Fsth\" alt=\"Age of the last signed tree head (live)\" /></a>\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/histor/actions/workflows/pages.yml\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/endpoint?url=https%3A%2F%2Falexar76.github.io%2Fhistor%2Fbadges%2Ftests.json\" alt=\"Tests (measured by CI)\" /></a>\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/histor/actions/workflows/pages.yml\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/endpoint?url=https%3A%2F%2Falexar76.github.io%2Fhistor%2Fbadges%2Fcoverage.json\" alt=\"Branch coverage (measured by CI)\" /></a>\n      <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/python-%3E%3D3.11-3776AB\" alt=\"Python >=3.11\" />\n      <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/store-Postgres%20%C2%B7%20SQLite%20dev-336791\" alt=\"Postgres in production, SQLite for development\" />\n      <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/labels-MTL%2F1%20on%20AWR%2F2-8d83ff\" alt=\"MTL/1 labels on AWR/2\" />\n      <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/log-RFC%209162-5fe3ff\" alt=\"RFC 9162 Merkle log\" />\n    everyone else is seeing.\n    \n    ## What it does\n    \n    ```mermaid\n    flowchart LR\n        R[\"Official MCP registry<br/>~21k servers\"] --> C[\"Crawler<br/>initialize + tools/list<br/>never a tool call\"]\n        C --> D[\"MTL/1 digest<br/>RFC 8785 + SHA-256\"]\n        D --> L[\"Four signed labels<br/>AWR/2 · did:key\"]\n        W[\"WARDEN sidecar<br/>published pattern set\"] --> L\n        L --> M[\"Merkle log<br/>RFC 9162\"]\n        M --> S[\"Signed tree head<br/>after every crawl\"]\n        M --> API[\"Desk · API · badge · Atom feed\"]\n        CL[\"Your client\"] -- \"tools it received\" --> K[\"/api/v1/check\"]\n        K -- \"signed: same · different · seen before\" --> CL\n        K -. \"opt-in digest count\" .-> M\n    ```\n    \n    - **Reads** every remote endpoint in the official registry: `initialize`, then `tools/list`\n      drained across pages. No tool is called, nothing is installed or executed, private addresses\n      are refused before a connection opens.\n    - **Also reads** a short list of popular remote servers the registry does not carry ([`histor/curated.json`](histor/curated.json), DeepWiki among them), under HISTOR's own namespace `urn:awr:mtl:1:registry:histor.modelmarket.dev/curated`, so no label claims a registry listing. When such a server publishes to the registry, the registry's listing replaces ours.\n    - **Runs npm and PyPI packages** — the servers people start locally with `npx` or `uvx` — in a [sandbox](docs/operations.md#package-sandbox): installed without running their code, started under gVisor with decoy credentials and no route out, read with `initialize` + `tools/list`, then up to 15 tools called once with canary arguments, inside the sandbox. gVisor's own trace says what the package did — programs started, names looked up, decoys opened — at install, at startup and when its tools were called. Completed observations are cached per published version; incomplete observations are retried; a new version that changes what its tools tell the model is a change in the log, like any endpoint's.\n    - **Digests** the tool set exactly as [MTL/1](https://github.com/alexar76/aicom/blob/main/awr/adoption/mcp-trust-label/PROFILE.md)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFour filings, zero merges: where three agents actually sit this week | TypeScript LibHunt (https://www.libhunt.com/posts/1545749-four-filings-zero-merges-where-three-agents-actually-sit-this-week)\nciteturn15search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; Zero-dependency TypeScript library. (by alexar76) ... HISTOR — public transparency log of MCP tool definitions: reads what remote MCP endpoints in the official registry advertise (never calls a tool), signs it as MTL/1 labels, appends them to an RFC 9162 Merkle log, and answers /check: is what a client received what was observed?\n\n  4. ### warden\n\n3 1 0 7.4 TypeScript\n\nWARDEN — MCP security firewall: vets an MCP server's tool definitions against static-scan rules, a signed threat feed, origin and tool-def pinning before any tool reaches the model. Zero-dependency TypeScript library. (by alexar76)\n\nImage: alexar76 logo\n\n> It scans advertised tool definitions — injection, exfiltration, secret requests — and records an allow or block before those definitions reach the model. It does not call the tools. Source: github.com/alexar76/warden (MIT). The Docker pull request pins the same version and lists nine tools, including vet_mcp_server and static_scan_tools.\n\n  5. ### histor\n\n4 1 0 5.5 Python\n\nHISTOR — public transparency log of MCP tool definitions: reads what remote MCP endpoints in the official registry advertise (never calls a tool), signs it as MTL/1 labels, appends them to an RFC 9162 Merkle log, and answers /check: is what a client received what was observed? Never calls a server safe.\n\nImage: alexar76 logo\n\n> HISTOR is the record of what a remote MCP server advertised, not a verdict that the server is safe. The desk is histor.modelmarket.dev. Source: github.com/alexar76/histor.\n\n  6. ### aimarket-hub\n\n5 3 0 2.1 Python\n\nAIMarket Hub — federated capability catalog, channels, invoke API, and plugins.\n\nNOTE: The number of mentions on this list indicates mentions on common posts plus user suggested alternatives. Hence, a higher number means a more popular project.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLog request: histor.modelmarket.dev/log (staging, 10qps list) - Participate - Witness-network mailing lists (https://lists.witness-network.org/mailman3/hyperkitty/list/participate%40lists.witness-network.org/thread/J5ZRRQ2EQRVIFF7LL23TWMTL4AVCLYNZ/)\nciteturn15search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: last week; Crawled: last week; Hello, I would like to request that HISTOR's log be added to the staging witness network, on the 10qps list. vkey histor.modelmarket.dev/log+ad3ca066+AfXpkWqXVW93sChXnhKsNzvGLTFAAredl1jLlEjbr4wU qpd 144 contact alexar76@rambler.ru Origin line: histor.modelmarket.dev/log (equal to the vkey key name).\n\n### Log request: histor.modelmarket.dev/log (staging, 10qps list)\n\n## Александр Артамохов\n\n30 Oct '26\n\n10:51 a.m.\n\nHello, I would like to request that HISTOR's log be added to the staging witness network, on the 10qps list. vkey histor.modelmarket.dev/log+ad3ca066+AfXpkWqXVW93sChXnhKsNzvGLTFAAredl1jLlEjbr4wU qpd 144 contact alexar76@rambler.ru Origin line: histor.modelmarket.dev/log (equal to the vkey key name). Key type 0x01, Ed25519. Checkpoint: https://histor.modelmarket.dev/checkpoint https://histor.modelmarket.dev/checkpoint Add-checkpoint rate: one request per witness every 10 minutes (144 per day), from a timer on the log's host. The log only grows; consistency proofs are served at https://histor.modelmarket.dev/api/v1/log/proof/consistency?first=&second= https://histor.modelmarket.dev/api/v1/log/proof/consistency?first=&second= and the witness client handles 409 by resubmitting from the witness's size. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAIMarket — live agent marketplace - Odel Module Marketplace (https://odel.app/modules/alexar76/aimarket-hub)\nciteturn15search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week;     io.github.alexar76/aimarket-hub\n\n## Deployment\n\nStart here: complete production deployment runbook. It is also available in Russian, Spanish, French and Chinese.\n\nThe runbook covers immutable commit-pinned releases, unprivileged systemd services, nginx/TLS on a hostname or `/hub` subpath, same-origin federation discovery and `invoke`, signed-manifest and real `402` assay evidence, protocol-only federation admission, UFW/Fail2ban/SSH hardening, backups, reboot acceptance, Alien Monitor and SKOPOS enrollment. Do not expose the provider backend or replace the Hub's Ed25519 key during a routine upgrade.\n\nReference record for the maintained public installation: `../docs/production-modelmarket-dev.md`.\n\n## Testing & coverage\n\nCI runs on every push (workflow); coverage badge is refreshed from `pytest --cov` on `main`.\n\nbash Copy\n    \n    `cd aimarket-hub\n    pip install -e \".[dev]\"\n    pytest tests/ -q --cov=aimarket_hub\n    `\n\n## Development\n\nbash Copy\n    \n    `pip install -e \".[dev]\"\n    `\n\nKey test modules: `test_api.py`, `test_crawler.py`, `test_plugin_system.py`, `test_channels.py`, `test_cross_hub_integration.py`\n\nAdd a plugin: create package under `../plugins/` with `pyproject.toml` entry point `aimarket.plugins`.\n\n* * *\n\n## Security\n\n  * SSRF protection on federation crawler (`crawler.py`)\n  * Hybrid signed evidence — with `AIMARKET_PQC=1`, manifests, discovery documents, invoke receipts, rejection receipts and Pay-on-Verified verdict envelopes carry Ed25519 and ML-DSA-65 signatures over the same versioned canonical payload. Classical verification remains mandatory; PQ verification fails closed when a PQ signature is present. The public `/ai-market/v2/receipts/verify` endpoint is pinned to this Hub's persisted keys and accepts no caller-supplied key, preventing self-verifying receipts (`signing.py`)\n  * Safety gate on every invoke (`safety_gate.py`)\n  * Verified, single-use stake deposits — in production every stake credit needs an on-chain deposit that pays the platform recipient, and the hash is burned by an atomic claim before the credit, so one deposit can never fund two publishers even under concurrent requests. The claim is keyed on the canonical transaction id (an EVM hash is case-insensitive at the JSON-RPC layer, so `0xAB…` and `0xab…` are one deposit, not two) (`supply_security.py`)\n  * Residual — stake deposits are not payer-bound. The stake verifier answers \"did somebody pay the platform?\", not \"did this publisher pay\", so whoever submits a matching hash first gets the credit. Binding it needs a publisher→wallet record the stake ledger does not yet have; channel deposits are already bound (see the entry below). Until then, treat a stake deposit hash as a bearer secret and submit it before it is public\n  * Single-use channel deposits + payer proof — a verified deposit funds exactly one channel and only for the wallet that signed for it (`channels.py`)\n  * Stake mutation is per-subject, slashing is operator-only — a shared token can neither credit a stranger's stake nor burn a rival's bond (`api.py`)\n  * Vulnerability reports: SECURITY.md → alexar76@rambler.ru\n\n## Related projects\n\nProject  | Relationship\n--- | ---\nAICOM / AI-Factory  | Ships products → hub index\naimarket-protocol  | Normative v2 spec\naimarket-sdks  | Client SDKs (Dart alpha)\naimarket-widget  | Embeddable UI\noracles  | Verifiable math capabilities — randomness, VDF, consensus, reputation (listed on hub)\ndesktop-integrations  | 8 Flutter consumer apps\nEcosystem architecture  | Full monorepo diagram\ndioscuri  | Twin community agents — MNEMOSYNE Q&A\n\n## Community\n\nThe DIOSCURI twins answer questions from synced GitHub docs.\n\nChannel  | Twin  | Best for\n--- | --- | ---\nDiscord  | Pollux  | Help, ideas, show-and-tell\nTelegram  | Castor  | Releases, digests, quick news\n\nEcosystem map: Alien Monitor · AICOM\n\n## License\n\nApache-2.0 — see LICENSE. Maintainers: CONTRIBUTORS.md.\n\n## Checked by Odel\n\n  * Endpoint answered on 18 Oct 2026\n  * Registry verified the namespace io.github.alexar76\n  * Repository reachable, not archived\n\n### Assessed by AI Jev\n\nHarmful\n    \n    8%\nFirst-party\n    \n    82%\nHigh impact\n    \n    100%\nAdult content\n    \n    1%\n\nRead from the listing, its tools and README on 25 Oct 2026. AI can make mistakes: a guide, not a check.\n\n## Requirements\n\nRuns\n    Remote, on modelmarket.dev\n\nTransport\n    Streamable HTTP\n\nSign-in\n    None\n\nCredentials\n    X-API-Key\n\nClients\n    Any MCP client\n\nhttps://modelmarket.dev/mcp\n\nThe publisher’s server itself; Odel doesn’t run it. Added to your modules, Odel fronts it with one address.\n\nThe registry says it needs a key; it answered Odel without one.\n\n## Details\n\nVersion\n    3.15.21\n\nUpdated\n    24 Oct 2026\n\nRepo created\n    22 May 2026\n\nLicense\n    Apache-2.0\n\nLanguage\n    Python\n\nGitHub\n    1 stars · 0 forks · 3 issues\n\nRegistry name\n    io.github.alexar76/aimarket-hub\n\n  * alexar76/aimarket-hub\n  * modelmarket.dev\n  * Registry listing--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n- Participate - Witness-network mailing lists (https://lists.witness-network.org/mailman3/hyperkitty/list/participate%40lists.witness-network.org/latest?count=50)\nciteturn15search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Hello, I would like to request that HISTOR's log be added to the staging witness network, on the 10qps list. vkey histor.modelmarket.dev/log+ad3ca066+AfXpkWqXVW93sChXnhKsNzvGLTFAAredl1jLlEjbr4wU qpd 144 contact alexar76(a)rambler.ru Origin line: histor.modelmarket.dev/log (equal to the vkey key name).\nWe’ll never know unless we give it a shot. Daniel Hill Arcaeon\n\nLog request: histor.modelmarket.dev/log (staging, 10qps list)\nby Александр Артамохов 04 Nov '26\n\nHello, I would like to request that HISTOR's log be added to the staging witness network, on the 10qps list. vkey histor.modelmarket.dev/log+ad3ca066+AfXpkWqXVW93sChXnhKsNzvGLTFAAredl1jLlEjbr4wU qpd 144 contact alexar76(a)rambler.ru Origin line: histor.modelmarket.dev/log (equal to the vkey key name). Key type 0x01, Ed25519. Checkpoint: https://histor.modelmarket.dev/checkpoint https://histor.modelmarket.dev/checkpoint Add